  <main>
    <section class="py-16 bg-white">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <p class="mb-8 rounded-md border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 p-4 text-gray-900"><strong>Takes effect January 1, 2027.</strong> This is version 2.2 of the Breeder/Seller Agreement. Until then, version 2.1 remains in effect: <a href="/legal/seller-agreement" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,45%)] underline">read version 2.1</a>.</p>

        <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900">Breeder/Seller Agreement</h1>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Effective Date:</strong> January 1, 2027 <strong>Version:</strong> 2.2</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">1. Introduction</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">This Breeder/Seller Agreement ("Agreement") governs your use of the BreederHQ Marketplace as a Breeder/Seller Provider. Subject to §11, by listing animals or breeding services on the BreederHQ Marketplace as a Breeder/Seller Provider, you agree to be bound by this Agreement in addition to the BreederHQ Terms of Service, the Acceptable Use Policy, the Marketplace Transaction Terms, and the Legal Definitions Schedule.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>BreederHQ is an introduction venue, not a party to your sales or services.</strong> BreederHQ introduces Buyers to you. It does not negotiate, set, approve, guarantee, or enforce the price, terms, conditions, warranties, health guarantees, deposits, reservation fees, refunds, delivery, or outcome of any agreement between you and a Buyer, and it is not a party to that agreement. You and the Buyer own your transaction and every dispute about it. Sections 5.6 and 7A explain what this means for you.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">This Agreement applies to Providers that hold a breeder account and whose Services-related activity involves the breeding, sale, transfer, or placement of animals (each, a "Breeder/Seller Provider"). Providers that hold a service-provider account to offer services to animals or animal owners are governed by the separate Service Provider Agreement.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Animals are listed, advertised, and offered for sale, placement, adoption for a fee, or deposit only by Breeder/Seller Providers, through a breeder account under this Agreement.</strong> A Service Provider account may not list or offer any animal in any form, and the Service Provider Agreement prohibits it. If you both provide services and sell or place animals, use your breeder account for the animal sales. This Agreement governs those sales, and the Service Provider Agreement governs any services you list separately under a service-provider account.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">"Provider," "you," and "your" refer in this Agreement to any individual or entity that lists animals or breeding services on the BreederHQ Marketplace as a Breeder/Seller Provider.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Capitalized terms used in this Agreement have the meanings given in the BreederHQ Legal Definitions Schedule, which is incorporated into this Agreement by reference.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">2. Eligibility</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.1 Requirements</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">To list on the BreederHQ Marketplace, you must:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Be at least 18 years of age (or the age of majority in your jurisdiction);</li><li>Have the legal authority to sell or offer the animals and breeding services you list;</li><li>Comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws regarding animal breeding, sales, and welfare;</li><li>Maintain all required licenses, permits, and registrations for your breeding operation;</li><li>Provide accurate and truthful account and business information;</li><li>Have the individual BreederHQ designates for your account pass the Identity Check described in §2.6 of the Terms of Service before any of your listings or your storefront is published, as set out in §2.3.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.2 Documentation Requests</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ may, in its sole discretion and from time to time, request from a Provider documentation supporting any representation the Provider has made on the Services, including without limitation representations of identity, business registration, breeding licenses, USDA certification, professional credentials, or animal pedigree and registration. <strong>The Provider's submission of requested documentation is a condition of continued marketplace participation; it is not a representation that BreederHQ has reviewed, validated, evaluated, or accepted the documentation for any purpose other than the Provider's continued marketplace participation.</strong> BreederHQ does not open, read, validate, compare, or vouch for any documentation submitted under this section. Failure to provide requested documentation within a reasonable time may result in suspension or removal of the Provider's listings. Submission of documentation under this section does not give rise to any duty on BreederHQ's part to detect, investigate, or remedy any defect in the documentation, nor to monitor the documentation for subsequent expiration or change. A documentation request under this section is separate from the Identity Check under §2.3: documentation submitted under this section does not satisfy or replace the Identity Check, and passing the Identity Check does not satisfy a documentation request.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.3 Identity Check</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">&gt; <strong>In plain terms:</strong> Before a storefront or listing can be newly published on the Marketplace, one person must pass an ID check run by our identity provider (today, Stripe Identity), using a picture of a government-issued photo ID and a live selfie. There is no other way to meet this requirement: BreederHQ does not review ID documents itself or offer a manual review or other alternative. For an account that belongs to a breeding program or business, that person is the account's owner; if the account has more than one active owner, it is the owner who was added first. A storefront or listing that was already public when this rule began may stay public during any transition period BreederHQ sets and, after that, unless and until BreederHQ unpublishes it; BreederHQ may then keep it unpublished until the check is passed. BreederHQ will ask that person, not anyone else, to agree to the check before it starts. BreederHQ's systems receive the result, not the ID or selfie images. As soon as the result is recorded, BreederHQ has the images and identity details deleted from its Stripe account and keeps only whether the check passed, the check's reference number, and its date (a reason a check did not pass may also appear for a short time in BreederHQ's operational logs and error reports); anything Stripe itself keeps is governed by Stripe's own policies (the Privacy Policy explains this). Your subscription and fees keep running while your storefront or listings wait for the check; if the check is not passed and you ask to cancel for that reason, your subscription and any listing subscriptions end that day, and the unused part of what you prepaid is refunded. Passing does not mean BreederHQ has checked you, your program, or your animals, and you may not say that it does. This box is a summary; the rest of this Section controls.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Passing the Identity Check described in §2.6 of the Terms of Service is a condition of publishing any animal listing, breeding-service listing, or storefront on the Marketplace. As of the effective date of this Agreement, the individual BreederHQ designates for your account (the "Designated Individual") is the account's owner (the "Account Owner"), as those terms are defined in the Legal Definitions Schedule. That individual must complete the Identity Check personally, using only their own genuine government-issued photo identification and their own live photo. BreederHQ may decline to publish, and may withdraw from public view, your listings and storefront while this condition is not met, as provided in §2.6 of the Terms of Service. A listing or storefront that was already public when this requirement first applied to you may remain public during any transition period BreederHQ sets under §2.6 of the Terms of Service, and otherwise until BreederHQ withdraws it; keeping it public during that time is not a breach of this Agreement.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Consent of the Designated Individual.</strong> Before the Identity Check begins, BreederHQ will ask the Designated Individual to consent to it, including to the Third-Party Identity Verification Provider's collection and comparison of their identification document and live photo. That consent is the Designated Individual's own to give. Your acceptance of this Agreement does not give it on their behalf, and you may not give it for them or complete the Identity Check in their place. If the Designated Individual does not consent, does not complete the Identity Check, or does not pass it, the condition in this Section is not met. BreederHQ does not review identification documents itself and does not offer a manual review, accommodation alternative, or any other way to satisfy this condition. If the Designated Individual cannot or will not complete the Identity Check, for any reason, your storefront and listings cannot be newly published on the Marketplace, any that remain public under the transition described above may be withdrawn, and your remedy is the cancellation and refund described in the next paragraph.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Fees while the condition is not met.</strong> Your access to the Marketplace is part of your BreederHQ subscription (§4.2), which also covers the rest of the Services under your plan. While your storefront or listings are unpublished or withdrawn because the condition in this Section is not met, your BreederHQ subscription and any listing subscription continue and are billed as usual; unpublishing does not pause, cancel, or reduce them. If the Designated Individual does not pass the Identity Check (including because they decline it or cannot complete it) and you want to cancel your BreederHQ subscription for that reason, you may ask BreederHQ, through the contact in §13, to cancel it immediately. BreederHQ will then end your BreederHQ subscription and every listing subscription on your account on the date of your request. None of them will renew after that date, and you will not be charged for any period after that date. BreederHQ will refund the unused portion of any prepaid BreederHQ subscription term and of each listing subscription ended under this paragraph, calculated by day from that date, together with the unused portion of any Boost or promotion fee you paid for a storefront or listing that could not be published, or was withdrawn, for that reason. One-time purchases, such as onboarding services, are not refunded under this paragraph. This paragraph does not apply if BreederHQ suspends or terminates your Marketplace access under §9 for fraud or misrepresentation in connection with the Identity Check.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The Identity Check is performed by the Third-Party Identity Verification Provider, not by BreederHQ, and any display of its result on the Services is a Third-Party Identity Verification Passthrough as described in §2.6 of the Terms of Service. <strong>Passing it is not BreederHQ's verification, vetting, approval, certification, or endorsement of you, your breeding program, your animals, or your listings, and BreederHQ does not vouch for or guarantee any of them.</strong> You may not state or imply, in your listings, storefront, communications with Buyers, or advertising on or off the Services, that BreederHQ has verified, vetted, approved, certified, or endorsed you, your breeding program, or your animals because the Identity Check was passed.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">3. Listing Standards</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.1 Accuracy</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">All listings must be truthful and accurate. You agree to:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Provide accurate descriptions of species, breed, age, sex, color, and markings;</li><li>Upload current, unaltered photos that accurately represent the animal or service;</li><li>Disclose all known health conditions, genetic test results, and medical history;</li><li>Accurately represent registration status and pedigree information;</li><li>State clear pricing, including any additional fees (shipping, health certificates, etc.);</li><li>Keep listings current and remove or update listings that are no longer available.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.2 Prohibited Listings</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You may NOT list:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Animals you do not own or do not have legal authority to sell;</li><li>Animals with known contagious diseases without full and prominent disclosure;</li><li>Animals obtained through theft, fraud, or illegal means;</li><li>Animals of species prohibited by federal, state, or local law;</li><li>Listings with intentionally misleading photos, descriptions, or health claims;</li><li>Animals involved in or bred for animal fighting or other illegal activities.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.3 Health Representations</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Any health claims, guarantees, or warranties you make in your listings or communications with Buyers are solely your representations. BreederHQ does not verify, endorse, or guarantee any health-related claims. You are responsible for backing up your health representations with appropriate veterinary documentation.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">4. Pricing and Fees</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">4.1 Listing Pricing</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You have sole discretion over the pricing of your animals and services. All prices must be listed in U.S. dollars unless otherwise specified.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">4.2 Platform Fees</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">By using the Marketplace, you agree to pay applicable BreederHQ platform fees, which may include:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Your BreederHQ subscription, which includes your access to the Marketplace as a Breeder/Seller Provider together with the rest of the Services under your plan (there is no separate subscription for Marketplace access), billed monthly or annually as you choose;</li><li>A listing subscription for a service listing you publish as a Breeder/Seller Provider (such as a stud, breeding, or other service listing), where BreederHQ charges a fee to publish that listing, billed monthly for each listing that carries one;</li><li>Boost or promotion fees for featured listing placement, where you choose to buy them; each is paid in advance for a fixed period and is not charged again automatically (if you turn on renewal, BreederHQ sends you a payment link when the period ends, and you are charged only if you pay it);</li><li>Transaction fees or commissions on completed sales, which BreederHQ does not currently charge and may introduce only as provided in paragraph (e) below.</li></ul>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Current prices and fee schedules are available on the BreederHQ website, at checkout, and in your account's billing settings. The following terms apply to your BreederHQ subscription and to any listing subscription (each, a "subscription"):</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(a) Billing and automatic renewal.</strong> A subscription is billed in advance at the start of each billing period to the payment method on file. A BreederHQ subscription's billing period is monthly or annual, as selected at checkout; a listing subscription's billing period is monthly. Charges are processed through BreederHQ's third-party payment processor, and any applicable tax is added. <strong>Each subscription renews automatically at the end of each billing period for another period of the same length, and is charged at the price then in effect for it, until you cancel it.</strong></p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(b) Free trials.</strong> If a subscription begins with a free trial, the length of the trial and the price that will be charged when it ends are shown at checkout. Unless you cancel before the trial ends, the subscription converts to a paid subscription and the first charge is made when the trial ends. If no payment method is on file when a trial ends, you are not charged, and the subscription does not continue as a paid subscription until you add one.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(c) How to cancel, and when cancellation takes effect.</strong> You may cancel your BreederHQ subscription at any time online, from the billing settings in your account; a user who holds the owner, administrator, or billing role on your account may do so. You may cancel a listing subscription at any time from that listing's billing settings. Cancellation takes effect at the end of the billing period or trial in which you cancel. The subscription will not renew, and no charge will be imposed for a renewal period beginning after the cancellation takes effect; amounts incurred before the cancellation takes effect remain due. You keep the access the subscription provides until the cancellation takes effect. Immediate cancellation with a refund is also available as provided in §2.3, which does not limit paragraph (d) or any right under applicable law.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(d) Refunds.</strong> Except as provided in this paragraph, in §2.3, and in §9.2(b) of the Terms of Service (termination without cause), in the terms of a particular offer presented to you at purchase, or where applicable law requires otherwise, fees are non-refundable, and canceling does not entitle you to a refund or credit for the remainder of a billing period or for an unused Boost or promotion. <strong>First-purchase guarantee.</strong> BreederHQ guarantees the first paid BreederHQ subscription on your Account for thirty (30) days. If you ask for a refund within thirty (30) days after the first charge for that subscription, BreederHQ will refund in full the subscription fee in that charge, with any tax charged on it, and cancel the subscription. Eligibility is measured by Account, meaning the BreederHQ account that holds the subscription, whether it belongs to an individual or to a breeding program, business, or other organization, and not by the individual who places the order or asks for the refund. The guarantee applies once per Account, and only to the first BreederHQ subscription for which that Account is charged. It does not apply to an Account that belongs to an individual or organization that has already received a refund under this guarantee on another Account. It does not apply to renewals, to any later subscription on the Account, to any listing subscription, to Boosts or promotions, or to one-time services, unless the terms of a particular offer presented to you at purchase say otherwise. Make the request through the contact method shown in your account's billing settings or on the BreederHQ website.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(e) Price and fee changes.</strong> BreederHQ may change its prices and fees, or introduce a new fee, with at least thirty (30) days' notice by email to the address on file and by in-product notification. A price change applies to an existing subscription only from the first renewal that begins after the notice period ends, and you may cancel under paragraph (c) before then to avoid it.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(f) After a subscription ends.</strong> When your BreederHQ subscription ends, your storefront and listings are removed from public view on the Marketplace and your access to the Services is limited until you subscribe again. When a listing subscription ends, that listing is removed from public view. Ending a subscription does not by itself delete your account or your data; the Privacy Policy describes how deletion works. You may subscribe again at any time from your account's billing settings.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(g) Disclosures at checkout.</strong> Before you start a subscription and before you are charged, BreederHQ will clearly present the terms in paragraphs (a) through (d), including the recurring price, the billing frequency, any trial and the price that applies when it ends, that the subscription renews automatically until canceled, how to cancel, and the refund terms, and will ask for your affirmative consent to them. After you subscribe, BreederHQ will send you an acknowledgment, in a form you can keep, that states those same terms, including the cancellation policy and how to cancel. BreederHQ will also send any reminder before a trial ends or a subscription renews that applicable law requires.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">4.3 Payment Processing</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Payments from Buyers are processed through our third-party payment processor. You agree to:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Maintain a valid account with our payment processor in good standing;</li><li>Provide accurate banking and tax information for payouts;</li><li>Comply with the payment processor's terms of service and acceptable use policy;</li><li>Accept that payment processing fees are separate from BreederHQ platform fees.</li></ul>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>BreederHQ's own role in payments.</strong> BreederHQ's role in payments is limited to the following. (a) BreederHQ charges you, through its third-party payment processor, for BreederHQ's own subscriptions, listing subscriptions, Boosts, promotions, and other fees under §4.2; BreederHQ is the seller of what those charges pay for, and §4.2 governs them. (b) BreederHQ supplies software that lets you request, accept, record, and refund payments from Buyers through your own account with the payment processor; when a Buyer pays you that way, the payment is made to you and processed by the payment processor under its terms. (c) Where a Buyer's payment is routed through BreederHQ's payment infrastructure, BreederHQ acts only as your limited payments agent as described in §2.7 of the Terms of Service and §2.2 of the Marketplace Transaction Terms. In none of these roles does BreederHQ decide whether a payment, deposit, reservation fee, or refund is owed between you and a Buyer, hold funds in escrow or trust, or become a party to your transaction.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">4.4 Payouts</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Payouts to your connected bank account are processed according to the payout schedule established in your payment processor account. BreederHQ does not control payout timing, holds, or reserves imposed by the payment processor.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">4.5 Chargeback and Dispute Liability</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">A payment for one of your transactions can result in a chargeback, reversal, payment dispute, or negative balance, whether the payment was made to your own account with the payment processor or was routed through BreederHQ's payment infrastructure on your behalf as described in §2.2 of the Marketplace Transaction Terms and §2.7 of the Terms of Service. Some of these can fall on BreederHQ's platform payment account, for example where a payment was routed that way or where the payment processor holds BreederHQ responsible for losses on your connected payment account. You acknowledge and agree that:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li><strong>You are solely responsible</strong> for any chargebacks, reversals, payment disputes, or negative balances arising from your transactions, regardless of how the payment was routed;</li><li>If a chargeback or dispute results in a financial loss to BreederHQ's platform payment account, you agree to <strong>promptly reimburse BreederHQ</strong> for the full amount of such loss, including the original transaction amount, chargeback fees, payment processor penalties, and any related costs;</li><li>BreederHQ may recover amounts owed by deducting from your future payouts, debiting your connected payment account, setting off against other amounts owed to you, invoicing you directly, or pursuing collection activities or legal action;</li><li>You agree to <strong>cooperate fully</strong> with BreederHQ and the payment processor in responding to chargebacks and disputes, including providing transaction records, communication logs, proof of delivery, and any other evidence reasonably requested;</li><li><strong>Failure to reimburse</strong> BreederHQ for chargeback losses within fifteen (15) days of notice may result in suspension or termination of your Marketplace access;</li><li>This obligation survives termination of this Agreement and your Marketplace account.</li></ul>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">5. Provider Obligations</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">5.1 Legal Compliance</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You are solely responsible for complying with all applicable laws, including but not limited to:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Federal Animal Welfare Act (if applicable to your operation);</li><li>State animal breeding and sales laws;</li><li>State consumer protection laws (including "puppy lemon laws" where applicable);</li><li>Local zoning and business licensing requirements;</li><li>USDA licensing requirements (if applicable);</li><li>State veterinary and health certificate requirements for animal transport;</li><li>Tax obligations that applicable law assigns to you, as set out in §10 of the Marketplace Transaction Terms;</li><li>Insurance coverage required by applicable federal, state, and local law for your operations; BreederHQ does not impose, require, evaluate, verify, hold, broker, or facilitate any such insurance, and your compliance with applicable insurance law is solely your independent legal responsibility.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">5.2 Animal Welfare</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You represent and warrant that:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>All animals in your care are housed, fed, and maintained in accordance with applicable animal welfare standards;</li><li>You do not engage in inhumane breeding practices, neglect, or cruelty;</li><li>Animals are provided appropriate veterinary care;</li><li>Breeding decisions are made with consideration for the health and well-being of the animals involved.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">5.3 Communication</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You agree to:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Respond to Buyer inquiries in a timely manner (within 48 hours is recommended);</li><li>Communicate honestly and transparently about animals and services;</li><li>Provide updates to waitlisted Buyers regarding expected availability, litter status, and selection processes;</li><li>Notify Buyers promptly of any material changes to a pending transaction.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">5.4 Fulfillment</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You are responsible for fulfilling all commitments made to Buyers, including:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Delivering animals as described in the listing and as agreed with the Buyer;</li><li>Providing registration paperwork, health records, and other promised documentation;</li><li>Honoring stated health guarantees or warranties;</li><li>Processing refunds in accordance with your published refund policy.</li></ul>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">5.5 Contract Preparation and Signing</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Terms of Service §7C governs contract templates, preparation, AI-assisted conversion, electronic signing, and related disputes. Templates are starting points, not legal advice. As between you and BreederHQ, you are solely responsible for the content, wording, accuracy, completeness, legality, and enforceability of Transaction Contracts you create, customize, import, or send, including system-template and AI-generated language you adopt. Arrange appropriate review by your own qualified counsel and verify the complete rendered document and its merged data before sending it. BreederHQ does not warrant the validity, enforceability, or suitability of a Transaction Contract or certify a signature's legal effect. BreederHQ's templates, editing tools, and AI-assisted conversion are not a substitute for the advice of an attorney.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You are responsible for identifying and satisfying the consumer-disclosure, delivery, signature, and retention duties that applicable law places on you. Do not rely on the ordinary electronic-signature checkbox as consent to receive legally required consumer records electronically. Where additional consumer consent is required, use a process that satisfies it, or supply the required records on paper in accordance with applicable law. Do not describe BreederHQ's templates or signing records as legal approval, identity certification, or a guarantee of enforcement.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">These obligations and disclaimers are subject to the limits, preserved rights, and prospective application in Terms of Service §§7C.6–7C.7 and §4.3. They do not excuse your duties to Buyers or transfer to Buyers responsibility for your contract drafting or statutory compliance.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">5.6 Your Agreements with Buyers; No Duty to Mediate</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(a) You and the Buyer own your agreement.</strong> You and each Buyer decide every term of your agreement, including price, deposit and reservation-fee terms, refund and cancellation terms, health guarantees and warranties, delivery and transport, and any return, rehoming, co-ownership, or breeding-rights terms, and you are responsible to the Buyer for performing what you agree to. BreederHQ does not negotiate, set, review, approve, guarantee, or enforce any of those terms, does not perform them, and is not a party to the agreement. A listing, storefront, message, waitlist, invoice, payment request, or other feature of the Services that displays or records a term you set does not make that term BreederHQ's.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(b) Contract tools are tools.</strong> BreederHQ's contract templates, editing tools, AI-assisted conversion, and electronic signing are tools that BreederHQ supplies. You and the Buyer choose and own the contents of any Transaction Contract between you. A template, including a template BreederHQ provides, is a starting point; it is not legal advice, not a recommendation that any term suits your transaction, and not a term of BreederHQ's. BreederHQ does not become a party to a Transaction Contract by supplying the tools used to prepare, sign, store, or display it, as provided in §5.5 and in §7C of the Terms of Service.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(c) No duty to mediate.</strong> BreederHQ has no duty to mediate, investigate, arbitrate, decide, or otherwise resolve any dispute between you and a Buyer or any other User. BreederHQ may choose, at its sole discretion, to help with a dispute, for example by passing along a message, providing records it holds, or acting on a report under the Acceptable Use Policy. Any such help is voluntary, may stop at any time, does not make BreederHQ a party to the dispute, and creates no obligation to help again or to reach any particular outcome. Action BreederHQ takes to enforce its own User Agreements, such as removing a listing or suspending an account, is not a decision of your dispute with a Buyer and does not affect your rights or the Buyer's rights against each other.</p>
