        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">7A. Release for Disputes Between Users</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(a) Release.</strong> To the fullest extent permitted by law, you release the BreederHQ Parties from all claims, demands, damages, losses, and liabilities of every kind, known or unknown, suspected or unsuspected, arising out of or in any way connected with a dispute between you and a Buyer or any other User, or with the acts, omissions, content, or conduct of a Buyer or any other User, including any agreement, transaction, booking, Transaction Contract, animal, service, payment, deposit, reservation fee, refund, meeting, or communication between you and them.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(b) California Civil Code §1542.</strong> You waive the protection of California Civil Code §1542, and of any similar law of any jurisdiction, to the extent it would otherwise limit the release in paragraph (a). Section 1542 provides: "A GENERAL RELEASE DOES NOT EXTEND TO CLAIMS THAT THE CREDITOR OR RELEASING PARTY DOES NOT KNOW OR SUSPECT TO EXIST IN HIS OR HER FAVOR AT THE TIME OF EXECUTING THE RELEASE AND THAT, IF KNOWN BY HIM OR HER, WOULD HAVE MATERIALLY AFFECTED HIS OR HER SETTLEMENT WITH THE DEBTOR OR RELEASED PARTY."</p>
